# BEGIN LOOM-MANAGED (merge drivers, #4528)
# install-metadata.json is a machine-local install stamp (loom_version,
# loom_commit, last_resync, loom_source) that every host's resync
# re-writes -- always keep our side on a merge conflict; the file is
# fully re-derived by the next resync regardless of which side "wins".
.loom/install-metadata.json merge=ours
# END LOOM-MANAGED (merge drivers, #4528)

# Layout streams are binary. Marked explicitly so no `text=auto` heuristic can
# ever line-ending-normalize one: a single byte changed in layout/*.gds breaks
# the content hash every flow/ evidence record cites for it, and the record
# would be reported stale rather than the corruption being reported as
# corruption. See flow/README.md, "The freshness rule".
*.gds binary
*.gds2 binary
*.oas binary
